{"schemaVersion":1,"moduleId":"food","status":"foundation","reviewStatus":"native-review-required","items":[{"id":"ceb_f_gusto_ko_og","module":"food","kind":"pattern","skill":"conversation","term":"Gusto ko og ___","meaning":"I want ___ / I would like ___","origin":"Spanish","example":"Gusto ko og tubig.","natural":"I would like water.","hint":"Gusto comes before ko. Og introduces the thing wanted; ug is a common spelling alternative.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Gusto","want / like"],["ko","I"],["og","object marker"],["tubig","water"]],"literal":"Want I [OBJ] water."},"accepted":["Gusto ko ug tubig"]},{"id":"ceb_f_dili_gusto","module":"food","kind":"pattern","skill":"conversation","term":"Dili ko gusto og ___","meaning":"I do not want ___","origin":"Mixed","example":"Dili ko gusto og kape.","natural":"I don’t want coffee.","hint":"Dili negates the following predicate. Og or ug introduces the thing not wanted.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Dili","not"],["ko","I"],["gusto","want"],["og","object marker"],["kape","coffee"]],"literal":"Not I want [OBJ] coffee."},"accepted":["Dili ko gusto ug kape"]},{"id":"ceb_f_kinahanglan","module":"food","kind":"pattern","skill":"conversation","term":"Kinahanglan ko og ___","meaning":"I need ___","origin":"Native","example":"Kinahanglan ko og tubig.","natural":"I need water.","hint":"Kinahanglan means needed or necessary. The needed thing follows og or ug.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Kinahanglan","need / necessary"],["ko","I"],["og","object marker"],["tubig","water"]],"literal":"Need I [OBJ] water."},"accepted":["Kinahanglan ko ug tubig","Kinahanglan nako og tubig"]},{"id":"ceb_f_naa_moy","module":"food","kind":"pattern","skill":"conversation","term":"Naa moy ___?","meaning":"Do you have ___? / Is ___ available?","origin":"Native","example":"Naa moy tubig?","natural":"Do you have water?","hint":"Moy is a common contraction of mo plus the linker -y. Naa introduces availability or existence.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Naa","there-is / have"],["mo-y","you-plural-LINK"],["tubig","water"]],"literal":"There-is you water?"},"accepted":["Naa mo'y tubig?","Aduna moy tubig?"]},{"id":"ceb_f_unsay_gusto","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Unsay gusto nimo?","meaning":"What would you like?","origin":"Native","example":"Unsay gusto nimo?","natural":"What would you like?","hint":"Unsay is unsa plus the linker -y. Nimo means your or by you in this construction.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Unsa-y","what-LINK"],["gusto","want"],["nimo","you / your"]],"literal":"What want your?"}},{"id":"ceb_f_usa_ka_botelya","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Usa ka botelyang tubig, palihug","meaning":"One bottle of water, please","origin":"Mixed","example":"Usa ka botelyang tubig, palihug.","natural":"One bottle of water, please.","hint":"Ka links the number to the counted item. Botelyang is botelya plus the linker -ng.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Usa","one"],["ka","count linker"],["botelya-ng","bottle-LINK"],["tubig","water"],["palihug","please"]],"literal":"One [COUNT] bottle water, please."},"accepted":["Usa ka botelya sa tubig, palihug","Usa ka tubig, palihug"]},{"id":"ceb_f_duha_ka","module":"food","kind":"pattern","skill":"conversation","term":"Duha ka ___","meaning":"Two ___","origin":"Native","example":"Duha ka kan-on, palihug.","natural":"Two servings of rice, please.","hint":"Use ka between a number and a counted noun or serving.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Duha","two"],["ka","count linker"],["kan-on","cooked rice"],["palihug","please"]],"literal":"Two [COUNT] rice, please."}},{"id":"ceb_f_usa_pa","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Usa pa","meaning":"One more","origin":"Native","example":"Usa pa, palihug.","natural":"One more, please.","hint":"Pa adds the sense of another or more.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Usa","one"],["pa","more / still"]],"literal":"One more."}},{"id":"ceb_f_tagpila_ni","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Tagpila ni?","meaning":"How much is this? / How much each?","origin":"Native","example":"Tagpila ni?","natural":"How much is this?","hint":"Tagpila often asks the price per item. Pila ni? is also natural when the per-item sense is not important.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Tag-pila","how-much-each"],["ni","this"]],"literal":"How-much-each this?"},"accepted":["Pila ni?","Tagpila kini?"]},{"id":"ceb_f_pila_tanan","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Pila tanan?","meaning":"How much is everything? / What is the total?","origin":"Native","example":"Pila tanan?","natural":"How much is the total?","hint":"Tanan means all or everything, so the phrase asks for the total price.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Pila","how-much"],["tanan","all / total"]],"literal":"How-much all?"}},{"id":"ceb_f_palit_ko_ani","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Palit ko ani","meaning":"I’ll buy this","origin":"Native","example":"Sige, palit ko ani.","natural":"Okay, I’ll buy this.","hint":"This compact market expression is common in conversation. Ani refers to this item.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Palit","buy"],["ko","I"],["ani","this / of-this"]],"literal":"Buy I this."},"accepted":["Mopalit ko ani","Kuhaon nako ni"]},{"id":"ceb_f_lami_kaayo","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Lami kaayo","meaning":"Very delicious / Really tasty","origin":"Native","example":"Lami kaayo!","natural":"It’s really delicious!","hint":"Lami means tasty; kaayo intensifies it.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Lami","delicious"],["kaayo","very"]],"literal":"Delicious very."}},{"id":"ceb_f_dili_halang","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Dili kaayo halang","meaning":"Not too spicy","origin":"Native","example":"Dili kaayo halang, palihug.","natural":"Not too spicy, please.","hint":"Dili kaayo softens the negative to not very or not too.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Dili","not"],["kaayo","very / too"],["halang","spicy"]],"literal":"Not too spicy."}},{"id":"ceb_f_walay_baboy","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Walay baboy, palihug","meaning":"No pork, please","origin":"Native","example":"Walay baboy, palihug.","natural":"No pork, please.","hint":"Walay means there is no or without. This is a compact request; explain allergies separately when safety matters.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Wala-y","none-LINK"],["baboy","pork / pig"],["palihug","please"]],"literal":"No pork, please."}},{"id":"ceb_f_para_diri","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Para diri","meaning":"For here / Eat here","origin":"Spanish","example":"Para diri lang.","natural":"For here, please.","hint":"Para is Spanish-origin and diri means here. Lang makes the reply softer.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Para","for"],["diri","here"],["lang","just"]],"literal":"For here only."},"accepted":["Diri lang"]},{"id":"ceb_f_bill_palihug","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Bill, palihug","meaning":"The bill, please","origin":"Mixed","example":"Bill, palihug.","natural":"The bill, please.","hint":"Bill commonly remains in English in natural Cebuano restaurant speech.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Bill","bill"],["palihug","please"]],"literal":"Bill, please."},"accepted":["Palihug ko sa bill","Bill palihug"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ari_bayad","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Ari ang bayad","meaning":"Here is the payment","origin":"Native","example":"Ari ang bayad.","natural":"Here’s the payment.","hint":"Ari draws attention to something being handed over; ang bayad is the payment.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Ari","here / here-it-is"],["ang","subject marker"],["bayad","payment"]],"literal":"Here [SUBJ] payment."},"accepted":["Mao ni ang bayad"]},{"id":"ceb_f_sukli","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Naa moy sukli?","meaning":"Do you have change?","origin":"Native","example":"Naa moy sukli?","natural":"Do you have change?","hint":"Sukli is the money returned after payment.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Naa","have / there-is"],["mo-y","you-LINK"],["sukli","change"]],"literal":"Have you change?"},"accepted":["Naa mo'y sukli?"]},{"id":"ceb_f_resibo","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Resibo, palihug","meaning":"Receipt, please","origin":"Spanish","example":"Resibo, palihug.","natural":"Receipt, please.","hint":"Resibo is Spanish-origin and widely understood.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Resibo","receipt"],["palihug","please"]],"literal":"Receipt, please."}},{"id":"ceb_f_wala_na","module":"food","kind":"phrase","skill":"conversation","term":"Wala na","meaning":"There is none left / It is no longer available","origin":"Native","example":"Wala na ang lechon.","natural":"There’s no lechon left.","hint":"Wala marks absence and na shows the new state: it is gone now.","analysis":{"tokens":[["Wala","none / absent"],["na","now / already"],["ang","subject marker"],["lechon","lechon"]],"literal":"Absent now [SUBJ] lechon."}}],"dialogue":{"title":"Ordering at Market Port","level":"Beginner 3","note":"This dialogue combines availability, quantity, spice preference, total price, and payment. Bill is retained as natural code-switching, while the core sentence structure remains Cebuano.","lines":[{"speaker":"A","text":"Maayong adlaw. Naa moy adobo?","tokens":[["Maayo-ng","good-LINK"],["adlaw","day"],["Naa","have / there-is"],["mo-y","you-LINK"],["adobo","adobo"]],"literal":"Good day. Have you adobo?","natural":"Good day. Do you have adobo?"},{"speaker":"B","text":"Naa. Unsay gusto nimo?","tokens":[["Naa","there-is"],["Unsa-y","what-LINK"],["gusto","want"],["nimo","you / your"]],"literal":"There-is. What want your?","natural":"Yes. What would you like?"},{"speaker":"A","text":"Usa ka adobo ug kan-on, palihug. Dili kaayo halang.","tokens":[["Usa","one"],["ka","count linker"],["adobo","adobo"],["ug","and"],["kan-on","cooked rice"],["palihug","please"],["Dili","not"],["kaayo","too"],["halang","spicy"]],"literal":"One [COUNT] adobo and rice, please. Not too spicy.","natural":"One adobo with rice, please. Not too spicy."},{"speaker":"B","text":"Sige. Usa ka gatos ka pesos tanan.","tokens":[["Sige","okay"],["Usa","one"],["ka","count linker"],["gatos","hundred"],["ka","count linker"],["pesos","pesos"],["tanan","total"]],"literal":"Okay. One hundred pesos total.","natural":"Okay. The total is 100 pesos."},{"speaker":"A","text":"Ari ang bayad. Salamat.","tokens":[["Ari","here"],["ang","subject marker"],["bayad","payment"],["Salamat","thanks"]],"literal":"Here [SUBJ] payment. Thanks.","natural":"Here’s the payment. Thank you."}]},"starterExercises":[{"id":"ceb_f_ex_01","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘I would like water.’","answerTokens":["Gusto","ko","og","tubig."],"wordBank":["tubig.","ko","Gusto","og","ka","pila"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_gusto_ko_og"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_02","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘Do you have water?’","answerTokens":["Naa","moy","tubig?"],"wordBank":["tubig?","moy","Naa","ko","og","pila"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_naa_moy"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_03","type":"choice","prompt":"What does ‘Unsay gusto nimo?’ mean?","answer":"What would you like?","choices":["What would you like?","How much is this?","Do you have change?","Where is the market?"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_unsay_gusto"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_04","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘One bottle of water, please.’","answerTokens":["Usa","ka","botelyang","tubig,","palihug."],"wordBank":["palihug.","tubig,","Usa","botelyang","ka","duha"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_usa_ka_botelya"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_05","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘How much is this?’","answerTokens":["Tagpila","ni?"],"wordBank":["ni?","Tagpila","tanan","ko","Naa","palihug"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_tagpila_ni"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_06","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘What is the total?’","answerTokens":["Pila","tanan?"],"wordBank":["tanan?","Pila","ni","ka","og","Gusto"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_pila_tanan"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_07","type":"choice","prompt":"Which phrase means ‘One more’?","answer":"Usa pa","choices":["Usa pa","Wala na","Para diri","Ari ang bayad"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_usa_pa"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_08","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘Not too spicy, please.’","answerTokens":["Dili","kaayo","halang,","palihug."],"wordBank":["palihug.","Dili","halang,","kaayo","Lami","ko"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_dili_halang"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_09","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘Here is the payment.’","answerTokens":["Ari","ang","bayad."],"wordBank":["bayad.","ang","Ari","sukli","ko","Pila"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_ari_bayad"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_10","type":"choice","prompt":"Which phrase asks whether the seller has change?","answer":"Naa moy sukli?","choices":["Naa moy sukli?","Pila tanan?","Wala na","Resibo, palihug"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_sukli"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_11","type":"sentence-builder","prompt":"Build: ‘No pork, please.’","answerTokens":["Walay","baboy,","palihug."],"wordBank":["palihug.","Walay","baboy,","halang","ko","Gusto"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_walay_baboy"]},{"id":"ceb_f_ex_12","type":"choice","prompt":"What does ‘Lami kaayo’ mean?","answer":"Really delicious","choices":["Really delicious","Not too spicy","One more","The bill, please"],"itemIds":["ceb_f_lami_kaayo"]}]}